# React — JSX Rules & Components as Functions

## 1. JSX kya hai?

JSX ka matlab hai **JavaScript XML**.

React mein JSX ki help se hum JavaScript file ke andar HTML jaisa syntax likh sakte hain.

```jsx
function App() {
  return (
    <div>
      <h1>Hello Abdullah</h1>
      <p>I am learning React</p>
    </div>
  );
}
```

JSX HTML jaisa dikhta hai, lekin ye JavaScript ke andar use hota hai.

---

## 2. JSX Rules

### Rule 1 — One Parent Element

Component ke `return` mein elements ko ek parent ke andar rakhna hota hai.

❌ Wrong:

```jsx
function App() {
  return (
    <h1>Hello</h1>
    <p>Welcome</p>
  );
}
```

✅ Correct:

```jsx
function App() {
  return (
    <div>
      <h1>Hello</h1>
      <p>Welcome</p>
    </div>
  );
}
```

---

### Rule 2 — `className` instead of `class`

HTML:

```html
<div class="container">
```

React JSX:

```jsx
<div className="container">
```

React mein CSS classes ke liye `className` use hota hai.

---

### Rule 3 — JavaScript inside `{}`

JSX ke andar JavaScript value use karne ke liye `{}` use karte hain.

```jsx
function App() {
  const name = "Abdullah";

  return <h1>Hello {name}</h1>;
}
```

Output:

```text
Hello Abdullah
```

---

### Rule 4 — Self-closing Tags

JSX mein self-closing elements ko `/` ke saath close karna hota hai.

```jsx
<img src="image.jpg" />
```

```jsx
<input type="text" />
```

```jsx
<br />
```

---

## 3. Components kya hain?

React application ko small reusable parts mein divide kiya jata hai.

In parts ko **Components** kehte hain.

Example:

```jsx
function Navbar() {
  return <nav>My Website</nav>;
}
```

Yahan `Navbar` ek React component hai.

---

## 4. Components as Functions

React mein component ek JavaScript function hota hai jo JSX return karta hai.

```jsx
function Welcome() {
  return <h1>Welcome to React</h1>;
}
```

Component ko doosre component mein use kar sakte hain:

```jsx
function App() {
  return (
    <div>
      <Welcome />
    </div>
  );
}
```

`<Welcome />` component ko render karta hai.

---

## 5. Component Naming Rule

React components ka naam **Capital letter** se start karna chahiye.

✅ Correct:

```jsx
function Navbar() {
  return <nav>Navbar</nav>;
}
```

```jsx
function UserCard() {
  return <div>User Card</div>;
}
```

❌ Avoid:

```jsx
function navbar() {
  return <nav>Navbar</nav>;
}
```

### Rule:

> React Component → Capital letter se start.

---

## 6. Import and Export

Agar component ko doosri file mein use karna ho to usay export karte hain.

### Navbar.jsx

```jsx
function Navbar() {
  return <nav>My Website</nav>;
}

export default Navbar;
```

### App.jsx

```jsx
import Navbar from "./components/Navbar";

function App() {
  return (
    <div>
      <Navbar />
    </div>
  );
}

export default App;
```

---

## 7. Real-World Component Structure

Ek real website ko multiple components mein divide kiya ja sakta hai:

```text
App
├── Navbar
├── Hero
├── Services
├── Portfolio
└── Footer
```

Example:

```jsx
function App() {
  return (
    <div>
      <Navbar />
      <Hero />
      <Services />
      <Portfolio />
      <Footer />
    </div>
  );
}
```

Is approach se code:

* reusable hota hai
* organized hota hai
* maintain karna easy hota hai
* large applications manage karna easy hota hai

---

## 8. Recommended Folder Structure

```text
src/
├── components/
│   ├── Navbar.jsx
│   ├── Hero.jsx
│   ├── Services.jsx
│   └── Footer.jsx
│
├── App.jsx
├── main.jsx
└── index.css
```

### `components/`

Reusable React components ke liye.

### `App.jsx`

Main application component.

### `main.jsx`

React application ko browser ke DOM se connect karta hai.

---

## 9. Complete Example

### Navbar.jsx

```jsx
function Navbar() {
  return (
    <nav>
      <h1>My Website</h1>

      <div>
        <a href="#">Home</a>
        <a href="#">About</a>
        <a href="#">Contact</a>
      </div>
    </nav>
  );
}

export default Navbar;
```

### App.jsx

```jsx
import Navbar from "./components/Navbar";

function App() {
  return (
    <div>
      <Navbar />
    </div>
  );
}

export default App;
```

---

## 10. Important Points

* JSX = JavaScript XML
* JSX HTML jaisa syntax provide karta hai
* JSX mein `class` ki jagah `className` use hota hai
* JavaScript values `{}` ke andar likhte hain
* Self-closing tags ko properly close karna hota hai
* React components usually functions hote hain
* Components JSX return karte hain
* Component names Capital letter se start hote hain
* Components ko `<Component />` ki tarah render karte hain
* `export default` component ko doosri file mein use karne deta hai
* `import` component ko doosri file se laata hai
* Large React applications ko reusable components mein divide kiya jata hai

---

## Practice

Create these components:

```text
components/
├── Header.jsx
├── Student.jsx
├── Course.jsx
└── Footer.jsx
```

Aur `App.jsx` mein:

```jsx
<Header />
<Student />
<Course />
<Footer />
```

use karo.

### Concepts Practiced

* JSX
* Components
* Functions
* `return`
* `import`
* `export default`
* Component rendering
* Folder structure
